  minimumAccusationEvidenceCount: 2
  correctResolutionSummary: 'Daniel Mercer killed Edmund Bellamy.

    

    Edmund
    had discovered Daniel''s financial fraud and intended to expose him the following
    morning.

    

    Daniel confronted Edmund in the Study. When Edmund refused
    to protect him, Daniel killed him with the heavy brass bookend.

    

    Daniel
    then attempted to conceal the financial motive and disturbed the document area
    to make the scene misleading.

    

    The evidence and witness information
    ultimately connected Daniel to the Study and the critical time surrounding Edmund''s
    death.'
  failedResolutionSummary: 'Your accusation was incorrect.

    

    The evidence
    did not support your conclusion, and the case of Edmund Bellamy''s death remains
    unresolved.'
