    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: cca31ea6e35ca6544a4ea42ef85ea3a4, type: 2}
    falseBeliefs: []
    allowedLieOrEvasionNotes: Daniel should remain controlled and professional. He
      may evade questions about company finances and falsely claim that he never
      entered the Study.
    temporaryHardCodedResponse: Of course, Detective. I'll answer what I can. I never
      went into the Study tonight.
  - npcDefinition: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9caf650e80c75824a98635ad24e114aa, type: 2}
    startingRoom: 5
    spawnPointId: adrian_npc_adrian
    knownFacts:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2e987dc32e1bbac4eb236e86144e39f8, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6d5d241d8263cf347b78bd6b9770e92b, type: 2}
    privateFacts:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6586c04fef993564ab79e59aab7f9978, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: eed6d705627dc8b4caf571ad92f7af9c, type: 2}
    falseBeliefs: []
    allowedLieOrEvasionNotes: Defensive and sarcastic when questioned about money
      or his argument with Edmund. He may initially avoid discussing his debt and
      the pawned family heirloom.
    temporaryHardCodedResponse: Ask what you need, Detective. My father and I argued,
      but that doesn't make me responsible for what happened.
  - npcDefinition: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5fbce395cd318be4786a3ff7be3ad048, type: 2}
    startingRoom: 3
    spawnPointId: kitchen_anna
    knownFacts:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9dc193700df9ab6488b5b4068b06d425, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 942d7ae1af09db7439f38352777efcfd, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 354faca25b6d7734ab94bd5592a00ecf, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6586c04fef993564ab79e59aab7f9978, type: 2}
    privateFacts: []
    falseBeliefs: []
    allowedLieOrEvasionNotes: Anna is practical and truthful. She must not identify
      the second person in the argument because she genuinely did not know who it
      was.
    temporaryHardCodedResponse: I heard Mr. Bellamy arguing with someone in the Study
      not long before I found him, but I couldn't tell who the other person was.
      I've kept the Study closed since then, but I can unlock it for you now, Detective.
  - npcDefinition: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d7fd2116d96c29f40b2917385cd3d954, type: 2}
    startingRoom: 1
    spawnPointId: dining_npc_secondary
    knownFacts:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 27d39c28e759d7747a8dc32b6daaec0f, type: 2}
    privateFacts:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 755882ef605b91b48bbccad1af29baab, type: 2}
    falseBeliefs: []
    allowedLieOrEvasionNotes: Direct and business-focused. She may be reluctant to
      discuss her plans to leave the company but can acknowledge that financial records
      had raised concerns.
    temporaryHardCodedResponse: There had been some tension at the company, Detective,
      but I don't know what happened in the Study.
  progressionRules:
  - ruleId: rule_anna_initial_conversation
    triggerNpc: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5fbce395cd318be4786a3ff7be3ad048, type: 2}
    requireInitialMeaningfulConversation: 1
    authoredClosingReveal: Detective, before you go... there is something I should
      tell you. The Study has been kept locked since Mr. Bellamy was found, so nothing
      inside would be disturbed. I heard him arguing with someone in there shortly
      before his death, but I couldn't identify the other person. I think you should
      examine the room yourself now. I'll unlock it for you.
    unlockRoom: 1
    roomToUnlock: 2
    discoverClue: 1
    clueToDiscover: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7227462e87bd9fe4bbaa71cd5f1b7b3d, type: 2}
